<section {{ cls }}="nx-container nx-article">
  <div>
    <h1 {{ cls }}="nx-title">About Nexy</h1>
    <p>
      Nexy puts the pages, the API and the interactive parts of a web app in one Python project.
      Backend developers keep the language they know, and the frontend keeps the tools it likes:
      {{ fw_label }}, Vite and hot reload.
    </p>
    <p>It is free and open source under the MIT license.</p>
    <div {{ cls }}="nx-actions">
      <a href="https://github.com/NexyPy/nexy#readme" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" {{ cls }}="btn-primary">Read the docs</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/NexyPy/nexy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" {{ cls }}="btn-ghost">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div {{ cls }}="nx-art">
    <img src="/hero-light.svg" alt="" {{ cls }}="nx-art-light" width="640" height="560" />
    <img src="/hero-dark.svg" alt="" {{ cls }}="nx-art-dark" width="640" height="560" />
  </div>
</section>
